The changes to it are structural. Markdown emits a flat list of sibling
elements, which is enough to style a document and not enough to say "the
section the pointer is in" or "the position being read". The builder now wraps
each heading-led run in a section and each position in an article, marks date
lines by their text, numbers every unit in reading order for the load-in
sequence, and splits labelled skill entries onto their own lines. All of it is
presentation the source file should not have to carry.

    build-pdf.py            written for this resume. Not derived from anything.

Everything else -- the stylesheets, the Justfile, the resume itself -- is my
own work.
